  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating COVID-19 recovery for vulnerable and marginalized groups in Cambodia through providing assets for poverty reduction and resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The COVID-19 pandemic brought substantive impact to Cambodia&#x2019;s economy and its people, particularly at-risk populations such as those living below or on the edge of the poverty line, workers in the informal sector (predominantly women), and individuals with disabilities. The project aims to improve the income-generating capacity of vulnerable rural households by supplying small-scale productive assets to improve the living conditions of impoverished households by providing goods that enhance the quality of life and healthcare, thereby improving hygiene practices.</narrative>
  </description>
